WEBVTT

00:01.290 --> 00:08.320
<i>Can you imagine a life where you 
can't even touch the person you love?</i>

00:09.130 --> 00:14.130
<i>The curse the witch laid upon him caused 
him to take the lives of any he touched.</i>

00:14.820 --> 00:19.150
<i>His own mother distanced herself from 
him, his friends called him a monster...</i>

00:19.150 --> 00:20.440
<i>Even people he'd never met spoke of him as</i>

00:20.440 --> 00:23.270
<i>"death incarnate that dwells in the forest."</i>

00:24.370 --> 00:29.250
<i>And yet, he doesn't feel 
the least bit lonely.</i>

00:31.900 --> 00:33.330
<i>I...</i>

00:36.350 --> 00:38.680
<i>I'm pretty lonely.</i>

00:44.410 --> 00:47.100
I'm jealous of you two.

00:48.090 --> 00:49.820
You have a family.

00:53.040 --> 00:55.030
It's been four days, huh?

00:55.380 --> 00:59.570
I didn't think we'd spend 
that much time at the circus.

00:59.570 --> 01:01.990
Rob must be worried.

01:02.500 --> 01:06.260
I hope Rob didn't decide to clean my room.

01:07.070 --> 01:09.960
He puts away things I need, you see.

01:09.960 --> 01:14.450
I cleaned it before we left, so it's fine.

01:14.910 --> 01:18.220
I moved what you were 
hiding under the bed, too.

01:19.040 --> 01:20.810
I don't hide anything under there.

01:22.310 --> 01:24.150
I don't, right?

01:24.490 --> 01:25.530
Alice?

01:25.530 --> 01:28.420
Why are you grinning, Alice?

02:59.030 --> 03:03.550
Episode 18
The Duke and Everyone's Daily Life

03:00.480 --> 03:01.740
We're back!

03:02.180 --> 03:03.950
Y-Young Master!

03:04.350 --> 03:06.910
I'm so glad... so glad you're safe!

03:07.930 --> 03:10.280
Don't try to give me a hug! It's dangerous!

03:10.280 --> 03:12.630
Sorry we were away for so long.

03:12.940 --> 03:18.330
No, it's a butler's job to watch 
the house while the master's away.

03:18.330 --> 03:20.150
Now once again...

03:20.150 --> 03:23.450
Welcome home, Young Master, Alice...

03:24.400 --> 03:26.080
We're back, Rob!

03:27.230 --> 03:30.520
I've finished my studies for the day.

03:30.940 --> 03:34.480
General education, politics, economics,

03:34.480 --> 03:37.880
linguistics, music lessons, golf lessons...

03:37.880 --> 03:40.380
I'm having no issues with any of them.

03:41.210 --> 03:41.910
I see.

03:51.210 --> 03:56.050
<i>By spring, the eldest will have 
lost his right to be heir,</i>

03:56.050 --> 03:58.300
<i>and I will be the one to 
inherit this household.</i>

03:59.600 --> 04:01.050
<i>But that's not good enough.</i>

04:01.980 --> 04:05.250
<i>I need to show that I'm better than him!</i>

04:05.700 --> 04:10.430
<i>I need to make Mother realize 
that I'm worthy to be heir.</i>

04:11.070 --> 04:13.800
<i>But there's no time left until spring.</i>

04:14.150 --> 04:15.440
<i>What do I do?</i>

04:16.260 --> 04:20.970
<i>Perhaps I could work on my makeup 
and try Operation Honeytrap 2?</i>

04:21.290 --> 04:24.660
<i>No... I hate the number two!</i>

04:26.330 --> 04:28.580
Hey, Brother Walter.

04:29.250 --> 04:31.290
Oh, Vio...la?!

04:32.290 --> 04:34.750
You said I've gained weight?

04:34.750 --> 04:38.250
Nah, you're just trying to get 
your hands on my macarons.

04:38.480 --> 04:41.010
You can't have even a single one!

04:41.010 --> 04:43.260
Look at your poor stockings!

04:44.070 --> 04:45.540
There's fat spilling out!

04:45.540 --> 04:47.770
Shut up. Don't be so loud.

04:48.100 --> 04:51.330
Who cares if I put on some weight?

04:51.330 --> 04:53.480
I'm a growing girl!

04:53.480 --> 04:56.800
I'm worried you'll damage your 
health by putting on weight!

04:56.800 --> 05:01.530
If you can't control yourself, you'll have 
no choice but to be your mother's slave!

05:02.810 --> 05:03.690
And...

05:04.040 --> 05:07.400
I'd assume Rob likes thin girls.

05:07.400 --> 05:08.070
Probably.

05:10.490 --> 05:11.910
I guess it's time for a diet!

05:12.350 --> 05:16.620
I'll cut out snacks, count calories...

05:16.620 --> 05:19.960
But what do I do to exercise?

05:19.960 --> 05:23.840
I'm no expert, so I can only 
tell you what I've heard.

05:23.840 --> 05:26.320
Do basic full body stretches consistently.

05:26.320 --> 05:28.650
Lift weights and engage in 
other anaerobic exercises.

05:28.650 --> 05:31.840
Add in walking and other aerobic exercises.

05:31.840 --> 05:34.060
Cut calories to a reasonable extent...

05:34.300 --> 05:36.320
I want a mille-feuille!

05:36.320 --> 05:38.230
I want a kouglof!

05:38.230 --> 05:40.270
You just started a diet a second ago!

05:40.270 --> 05:44.720
There are a few advantages to 
packing on some pounds, you know.

05:44.720 --> 05:47.240
See? I've got boobs!

05:47.240 --> 05:51.490
Touch them while you can. Once you 
lose weight, they'll disappear.

05:51.490 --> 05:53.310
Good idea, Viola!

05:53.310 --> 05:55.830
Each time you kick me, it burns calories!

05:55.830 --> 05:58.070
More! Kick me!

05:58.070 --> 06:00.440
Now hit me! Hard!

06:00.440 --> 06:01.900
Good! Good!

06:02.630 --> 06:04.250
Good! Good!

06:05.120 --> 06:09.760
Fifteen, sixteen, seventeen...

06:09.760 --> 06:10.830
I can't do it anymore.

06:10.830 --> 06:12.970
Weightlifting's the most 
boring thing in the world.

06:12.970 --> 06:14.350
Just at first!

06:14.350 --> 06:15.670
When you get used to it, it's fun.

06:15.670 --> 06:17.430
Don't sit in front of me.

06:18.920 --> 06:20.400
Don't look at me.

06:22.340 --> 06:25.270
No more! I'm tired! I can't go on!

06:25.270 --> 06:29.800
Legs up high! Move your arms! Back straight!

06:29.800 --> 06:31.880
But I can't...

06:34.620 --> 06:38.640
Nobody will listen to your romantic 
advice if you don't straighten up!

06:38.640 --> 06:40.550
Get to work!

06:41.290 --> 06:42.790
Shut up!

06:43.160 --> 06:45.390
Forget the diet!

06:45.390 --> 06:50.010
Rob will understand even if I'm a bit chubby!

06:51.590 --> 06:53.140
I don't want you to give up.

06:55.290 --> 06:58.280
It's easy to just go with 
the flow. It feels good.

06:58.600 --> 07:02.890
But there are times when you have to hang
 in there if you want to change something.

07:04.980 --> 07:09.660
I know that you work harder 
than anybody, Viola!

07:11.240 --> 07:12.780
What's wrong, Viola?

07:13.610 --> 07:19.620
Mom got mad and said I had to play 
as good as my eldest brother!

07:19.620 --> 07:21.520
Him again?

07:21.520 --> 07:26.890
Dear Brother Walter, I'll do my best until 
I can play good, so practice with me!

07:27.940 --> 07:30.470
You're a person who can work 
hard when nobody's watching.

07:30.750 --> 07:32.660
So don't give up.

07:33.100 --> 07:34.930
Don't let your laziness win!

07:35.240 --> 07:37.390
You can do it! I know you can!

07:37.390 --> 07:38.970
You can do it, Viola!

07:38.970 --> 07:40.370
You can do it, Viola!

07:40.370 --> 07:43.430
You can do it, Vio...la!

07:43.430 --> 07:44.650
Fine!

07:45.120 --> 07:47.570
I'll do my best, for Rob.

07:47.840 --> 07:49.530
So leave me alone for a little.

07:49.530 --> 07:51.710
Of course. I'll be cheering you on!

07:57.030 --> 07:58.810
I won't lose either...

07:59.250 --> 08:05.000
I need to prove that I'm better 
than my clueless eldest brother!

08:07.690 --> 08:09.460
I could go into town!

08:11.160 --> 08:13.930
Look at all this junk.

08:14.520 --> 08:16.440
Is there more here than there used to be?

08:16.920 --> 08:19.140
I can't throw away a gift, you see.

08:19.590 --> 08:23.100
True, some of this I gave to you...

08:24.170 --> 08:27.200
There really is a lot here.

08:32.340 --> 08:34.820
Look at this, Alice!

08:35.240 --> 08:36.410
Ta-dah!

08:36.410 --> 08:40.540
A collection of illustrations that the Young 
Master drew when he was little!

08:40.900 --> 08:42.820
Why do you have that?

08:42.820 --> 08:44.250
I'd love to see it.

08:44.650 --> 08:48.090
Then you may have it.

08:48.390 --> 08:50.710
Don't give her that! That's mine!

08:51.760 --> 08:54.420
Should I give it back to you?

08:54.810 --> 08:57.140
Y-You can have it, Alice!

08:57.140 --> 08:58.840
Thank you!

08:58.840 --> 09:00.840
He's always so easily persuaded.

09:00.840 --> 09:02.100
You don't get to talk!

09:04.490 --> 09:08.560
I have gifts for you from Circus Gemini!

09:08.560 --> 09:10.890
From the Circus?

09:10.890 --> 09:13.780
I've never even met them. That's so kind!

09:14.310 --> 09:17.280
First, from the Ringmaster, 
tickets to the circus.

09:17.990 --> 09:20.740
From Hugo, a signed bottle cork.

09:20.740 --> 09:24.160
He was telling me that he'll be the 
greatest entertainer in the world someday,

09:24.160 --> 09:25.390
and it'll be worth something then.

09:26.130 --> 09:27.940
I'll look forward to that!

09:27.940 --> 09:30.460
Cuff gave you this rock 
that looks like a cat.

09:30.940 --> 09:33.280
She said she liked it and 
was carrying it for a while,

09:33.280 --> 09:34.670
but she'd make a special gift of it for you.

09:35.000 --> 09:37.970
What a kind soul!

09:37.970 --> 09:41.890
The other members of the circus gave me a 
bunch of stuff too, so I brought it all!

09:41.890 --> 09:45.100
It's all wonderful. I love it.

09:45.410 --> 09:49.220
And from Zain, a small spyglass.

09:49.220 --> 09:52.070
It's light and might be 
good for birdwatching.

09:53.700 --> 09:54.780
What's this?

09:55.280 --> 09:56.640
Can you see?

09:56.640 --> 09:58.490
You're all I can see...

09:59.280 --> 10:01.950
I have a gift for you as well, Rob.

10:02.570 --> 10:03.880
What could it be?

10:03.880 --> 10:07.400
Coffee beans. I'm sorry it's not 
as interesting as the others.

10:07.400 --> 10:11.960
Why are you apologizing? You're cute,
 so everything you do is okay!

10:12.570 --> 10:15.170
And I got you a new chessboard!

10:15.170 --> 10:17.210
Well? Do you like it?

10:17.210 --> 10:18.900
Oh!

10:18.900 --> 10:24.230
My deepest gratitude to you two 
and the members of the circus!

10:24.230 --> 10:27.050
I'm a happy man.

10:27.050 --> 10:28.560
That's great!

10:28.930 --> 10:31.330
Hey, why don't we play a game of chess?

10:31.330 --> 10:33.740
Oh, of course.

10:33.740 --> 10:35.970
I'll prepare some sweet snacks.

10:35.970 --> 10:38.530
Thank you.

10:45.400 --> 10:47.410
<i>Perhaps it seems...</i>

10:48.380 --> 10:51.350
<i>I'm not as lonely as I thought.</i>

10:52.750 --> 10:56.090
<i>I really am a lucky man.</i>

11:20.680 --> 11:22.120
They kissed!

11:22.450 --> 11:24.260
Did you see that, Hugo?

11:24.260 --> 11:26.610
Yeah! They're so cute!

11:26.610 --> 11:29.120
<i>Hmph. There goes our time alone.</i>

11:30.570 --> 11:32.520
<i>I was supposed to go on a date today,</i>

11:32.520 --> 11:36.010
<i>but the ringmaster wants me 
to find an idea for a new act,</i>

11:36.810 --> 11:38.890
<i>and a third wheel decided to tag along.</i>

11:40.050 --> 11:42.050
<i>This was supposed to be 
our first official date,</i>

11:42.050 --> 11:43.830
<i>but it's not romantic at all.</i>

11:43.830 --> 11:45.510
<i>It really is a date, right?</i>

11:46.240 --> 11:48.640
<i>There's nothing exciting 
about looking at animals.</i>

11:48.640 --> 11:48.970
Here!

11:52.860 --> 11:55.450
Well, I guess it's not that bad.

11:55.860 --> 12:00.400
I don't know what Daleth is 
going to do next, though.

12:00.890 --> 12:04.410
I used my time magic, like she wanted.

12:05.840 --> 12:08.260
But what is she after, anyway?

12:08.860 --> 12:12.670
How does she benefit from me using my magic?

12:13.530 --> 12:17.980
She'd said something about waking Alice's 
mother up from her slumber, I guess.

12:17.980 --> 12:19.920
But I can't trust that.

12:22.320 --> 12:24.550
What are you frowning at?

12:25.050 --> 12:27.510
Let's look at the animals together, Zain!

12:27.510 --> 12:28.660
Sure thing!

12:28.660 --> 12:30.300
Can I give you a hug?

12:30.300 --> 12:32.160
Stop right there, sex monster!

12:32.570 --> 12:34.700
Come on, to the next area!

12:34.700 --> 12:35.690
Ow...

12:50.970 --> 12:52.410
Look, Zain!

12:52.410 --> 12:54.660
They like me!

12:57.500 --> 13:00.230
Stop looking at Cuff with 
those dirty eyes of yours!

13:00.230 --> 13:03.410
Stop hitting me all the time!

13:03.410 --> 13:04.970
I'm her boyfriend, you know.

13:04.970 --> 13:08.570
You were only able to ask her 
out because I gave you a push.

13:08.570 --> 13:10.260
I am grateful for that.

13:10.260 --> 13:11.670
Thanks!

13:11.670 --> 13:13.290
Aw, you're so cute!

13:13.290 --> 13:15.640
I'm not going to get in your way,

13:16.260 --> 13:18.110
but I like Cuff, too.

13:18.460 --> 13:21.060
And I don't have anybody else to play with.

13:21.400 --> 13:23.370
What about your pickpocketing buddies?

13:23.880 --> 13:25.910
I cut ties with them a long time ago.

13:25.910 --> 13:29.830
Some of them are mad at me for leaving,

13:30.270 --> 13:31.830
but I don't care anymore!

13:32.950 --> 13:35.990
So let me hang out with you 
guys once in a while, okay?

13:35.990 --> 13:37.720
And take good care of Cuff.

13:37.720 --> 13:40.590
Yeah, I sure will.

13:46.410 --> 13:47.960
The lion cage!

13:47.960 --> 13:48.740
What?

13:49.610 --> 13:54.300
Zain, did you know they call the 
lion the king of the beasts?

13:54.300 --> 13:56.580
You're really smart, Cuff.

13:57.850 --> 13:59.850
This sure is popular, though.

13:59.850 --> 14:02.570
We can barely see anything.

14:03.740 --> 14:04.520
Here.

14:04.980 --> 14:06.310
Now you can see, right?

14:06.310 --> 14:08.370
Yeah! Thanks, Zain!

14:08.370 --> 14:09.130
Huh?

14:09.130 --> 14:09.990
What's wrong?

14:10.300 --> 14:13.730
Nothing, just... I've 
never seen a lion before.

14:13.730 --> 14:15.700
Is that really a lion?

14:22.730 --> 14:26.340
"Lion the red panda, everybody's friend."

14:27.370 --> 14:29.050
Don't give the animals confusing names!

14:32.650 --> 14:35.130
Are you going to see Alice and the Duke?

14:35.130 --> 14:38.980
Yeah, the circus is closed tomorrow.

14:39.260 --> 14:41.400
We need to go see them 
when we've got a chance.

14:41.400 --> 14:43.950
I want to talk with Alice a whole bunch!

14:44.380 --> 14:49.150
Okay, I won't bother you guys anymore!

14:49.150 --> 14:51.200
See you tomorrow, Cuff!

14:51.200 --> 14:53.370
Zain, don't get too out of control!

14:53.370 --> 14:54.730
Bye!

14:55.860 --> 14:58.580
What was that supposed to mean?

14:59.320 --> 15:01.790
Our date was a lot of fun, right, Zain?

15:02.390 --> 15:03.630
Can I kiss you?

15:03.630 --> 15:04.250
No.

15:04.830 --> 15:06.340
Let me feel your tits, then.

15:09.910 --> 15:12.050
You ruined it, Zain.

15:12.400 --> 15:14.680
You're such a dork.

15:40.890 --> 15:42.060
You saw!

15:43.640 --> 15:45.990
Somebody saw my face...

15:46.890 --> 15:49.090
And after I worked so hard to hide it!

15:49.800 --> 15:53.120
This ugly face...

15:53.600 --> 15:56.270
These wounds that even magic can't heal...

15:57.270 --> 16:01.240
Do you understand how lonely I am,

16:03.020 --> 16:03.880
my sister?

16:09.060 --> 16:11.780
Man, just our luck.

16:12.160 --> 16:13.920
It was a clear sky.

16:13.920 --> 16:15.990
I didn't expect it to 
suddenly become a blizzard.

16:16.700 --> 16:19.410
I guess the weather changes 
easily on the mountain.

16:19.410 --> 16:22.410
And I was looking forward to seeing Alice.

16:23.330 --> 16:24.320
Yeah.

16:24.320 --> 16:26.730
We won't be able to make it like this.

16:27.820 --> 16:30.200
I'd like to go back to town when it stops,

16:30.200 --> 16:32.920
but I guess we'll have 
to stay here for a while.

16:35.910 --> 16:37.810
Take my jacket.

16:37.810 --> 16:39.660
No, I'm not cold.

16:40.000 --> 16:43.110
No, I can see through your clothes!

16:43.840 --> 16:46.360
Or can I stare?

16:46.360 --> 16:47.950
Of course not.

16:48.400 --> 16:50.780
I'll use magic to dry it. 
I don't need your jacket.

16:56.690 --> 16:59.800
It's been a while since it's 
been just the two of us.

16:59.800 --> 17:01.120
Yeah.

17:01.120 --> 17:04.250
Hugo or somebody else from 
the circus is always around.

17:05.250 --> 17:06.390
<i>Our first night...</i>

17:06.390 --> 17:08.330
<i>...together as lovers.</i>

17:08.630 --> 17:10.320
<i>So romantic.</i>

17:10.320 --> 17:11.460
<i>So hot.</i>

17:12.010 --> 17:15.890
Zain, since we're alone, why don't we do 
something only the two of us could do?

17:16.510 --> 17:17.600
Something sexy?

17:17.600 --> 17:19.180
No. I'll hit you again if you keep that up.

17:19.480 --> 17:21.160
Be gentle, at least!

17:21.160 --> 17:22.270
Just watch.

17:23.930 --> 17:25.730
Guess what this animal is.

17:26.230 --> 17:27.320
A fox?

17:27.650 --> 17:28.960
I remember this.

17:28.960 --> 17:31.210
We used to play this game all 
the time when we were kids.

17:31.210 --> 17:32.000
Yeah.

17:32.000 --> 17:32.940
Let's play some more.

17:39.490 --> 17:49.620
<i>When you remember an old story</i>

17:49.620 --> 17:56.700
<i>Magic animals come dancing out of nowhere</i>

17:56.700 --> 18:02.640
<i>Let's draw them with shimmering flames</i>

18:02.640 --> 18:08.360
<i>Foxes, lions, red pandas</i>

18:03.900 --> 18:05.740
Camel, hippo...

18:05.740 --> 18:07.600
And that's a monkey and a bird?

18:08.360 --> 18:14.230
<i>Camels, zebras, monkeys and hippos</i>

18:08.610 --> 18:10.530
Those are all animals we saw today.

18:11.330 --> 18:13.700
I thought I'd draw them while 
I still remembered them.

18:14.040 --> 18:15.570
What's this, then?

18:14.230 --> 18:19.390
<i>All glowing with gentle light</i>

18:18.760 --> 18:19.780
It's Alice!

18:19.390 --> 18:26.390
<i>I'm not lonely, because I'm not alone</i>

18:19.780 --> 18:22.410
Ow!

18:21.120 --> 18:23.000
Why would you touch it?

18:23.000 --> 18:24.080
I couldn't help myself.

18:24.790 --> 18:30.290
Zain, when we were at the zoo, you 
were thinking about Daleth, right?

18:26.390 --> 18:30.290
<i>If together, we can bring light</i>

18:30.560 --> 18:37.710
<i>Bring hope to a place with nothing at all</i>

18:31.450 --> 18:33.570
Yeah, a little.

18:34.140 --> 18:37.010
I'm wondering what her next move is.

18:37.710 --> 18:42.630
<i>we can do anything</i>

18:38.080 --> 18:39.310
Don't worry.

18:39.650 --> 18:42.630
If something happens, 
I'll protect you with my magic.

18:42.630 --> 18:45.950
It's the other way around. I'll protect you.

18:43.470 --> 18:50.970
<i>We'll always be together</i>

18:45.950 --> 18:46.850
Okay.

18:46.850 --> 18:48.940
I'll protect everyone, then.

18:50.970 --> 18:55.150
Do you regret using your time magic?

18:55.420 --> 18:56.230
No.

18:56.230 --> 18:58.310
I did it to protect you.

18:59.300 --> 19:01.870
My weird feelings about it all disappeared.

19:02.700 --> 19:03.590
I see.

19:04.380 --> 19:06.610
I won't know if I can do it until I try,

19:06.610 --> 19:12.300
but I'm thinking of going back in time to 
stop the curse from being placed on him.

19:12.300 --> 19:14.290
Can you do that?

19:14.850 --> 19:16.970
Like I said, I won't know till I try.

19:17.460 --> 19:20.470
I wasn't able to bring our 
parents back to life, after all.

19:21.110 --> 19:23.010
You can't change fate.

19:25.400 --> 19:26.400
But...

19:26.400 --> 19:29.130
If his curse isn't fate,

19:29.580 --> 19:31.690
then there's a chance.

19:32.270 --> 19:34.630
I'm not sure I really understand.

19:34.630 --> 19:35.400
But okay.

19:35.400 --> 19:40.970
The biggest problem is that we'll have to 
fight the person who put the curse on him.

19:40.970 --> 19:43.830
Daleth's sister, Sade.

19:45.260 --> 19:50.550
Whether we can beat the one that they called 
the strongest, most terrible Witch...

19:50.550 --> 19:54.660
Don't worry! I'll get stronger!

19:54.660 --> 19:56.790
So don't worry about it, 
no matter who I'm facing.

19:57.500 --> 19:59.760
I'm so proud I could cry.

20:00.270 --> 20:02.020
Can I kiss you?

20:02.020 --> 20:03.210
No.

20:04.760 --> 20:07.230
They're dear friends.

20:07.230 --> 20:09.200
I want to break the curse as soon as I can.

20:11.310 --> 20:12.260
Yeah.

20:12.260 --> 20:16.360
And we have to repay the ringmaster 
and the others, little by little.

20:17.370 --> 20:18.660
Hey, Zain.

20:18.990 --> 20:20.070
What?

20:24.070 --> 20:27.250
If the blizzard never stopped, ever,

20:27.250 --> 20:29.590
and it was just the two 
of us alone forever...

20:29.590 --> 20:30.600
What would you do?

20:39.230 --> 20:41.280
D-Don't be stupid!

20:41.280 --> 20:44.830
It'll clear up by morning, and then
we can head back to town!

20:44.830 --> 20:46.640
Yeah. You're right.

20:47.700 --> 20:52.100
<i>If... If the blizzard 
really never did stop...</i>

20:53.020 --> 20:56.440
<i>I'd... work up the courage, and...</i>

21:00.510 --> 21:02.110
Look, Zain!

21:02.110 --> 21:04.010
I cleared up after all!

21:04.010 --> 21:05.570
Yeah.

21:06.360 --> 21:08.530
Of course it did, yeah.

21:09.090 --> 21:12.200
I'm hungry. Let's go home and eat.

21:12.200 --> 21:13.250
Right, right.

21:18.690 --> 21:20.140
What was that for?

21:20.850 --> 21:24.590
I'm not sure when we'll 
be alone together again.

21:25.260 --> 21:28.080
But you get mad when I try to touch you!

21:28.080 --> 21:29.760
What, did it make you upset?

21:29.760 --> 21:32.060
No, it made me really happy!

21:32.650 --> 21:35.020
Do it again sometime...

23:07.280 --> 23:09.980
My diet's complete!

23:10.490 --> 23:14.930
Time to eat some macarons as a 
reward for losing weight!

23:14.930 --> 23:16.950
You'll just go back to how you were, right?

23:16.950 --> 23:19.330
It's just one!

23:20.090 --> 23:25.160
Hey, Dear Brother, thanks for inspiring me.

23:26.400 --> 23:29.170
Here. I'll give you one. Just one.

23:29.630 --> 23:30.610
No thanks.

23:30.610 --> 23:32.010
I'm trying to avoid sweets.

23:32.010 --> 23:33.450
Jerk!

23:35.010 --> 23:40.250
The Duke of Death and His Maid
The Duke, Alice, and the Encounter in the Witches' World

23:35.510 --> 23:39.610
"The Duke, Alice, and the 
Encounter in the Witches' World."
